{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-66b5f2f7-bef6-4143-94b5-b812a11c1d4f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8ccc01b40b9db15","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-bzt_4ujg/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-E001.md","content":"# Keyboard operability and focus indicator remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic remediates the keyboard accessibility defects identified by the\naccessibility audit in the four core Dashboard flows: project creation, workbench\nspawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. On completion, each of the four\nflows can be completed end-to-end with keyboard alone — no focus traps, no\nunreachable controls — and focus indicators are visibly consistent across all\naudited surfaces. This epic delivers the code-side fix state that the updated\nconformance documentation will describe.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Fix focus-loss and focus-trap defects in the modals and dialogs of the four\n  audited flows, per the defect list enumerated in the audit report.\n- Make all controls reachable in the audited flows that the audit marked as\n  keyboard-unreachable.\n- Normalize visible focus indicators across the audited flows so focus state is\n  consistent (same visual treatment on equivalent controls) throughout.\n- Cover the four audited flows only; flows and screen-reader semantics outside the\n  audit scope are explicitly out of scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed start to finish using\n  keyboard input alone, verified by exercising every step of the flow.\n- No control in the audited flows is unreachable via keyboard navigation\n  (tab/shift-tab/arrow keys/enter/escape as applicable to each control type).\n- Focus is never lost or trapped: opening and closing any modal or dialog in the\n  audited flows returns focus to the invoking element, and focus order follows the\n  visual/logical order of the page.\n- Focus indicators are visibly consistent: equivalent controls across the four\n  audited flows show the same focus indicator treatment, and every focusable\n  control shows a discernible focus indicator.\n- Every defect enumerated by the audit report for the four flows is addressed or\n  explicitly dispositioned with rationale.\n- Keyboard regression checks for the four flows are added to the Dashboard test\n  suite so the fixes are guarded against regressions.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard, with\n  no focus traps or unreachable controls — delivered by the focus-trap,\n  focus-loss, and reachability fixes above.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n  flows — delivered by the focus indicator normalization above, bundled with HLR-1\n  because both edit the same flows, dialogs, and UI surfaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24015,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8110d2cf8b5bd911","agent_id":"a66b0586c2e4bfdbd","session_id":"73162c37-dfef-4424-b9a3-b9a22025d187","uuid":"f5dce977-9471-4217-a2de-b6f89ac15791","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:46:41.967Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
