{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9395bd3289926d98","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tepic_count: 2\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9017\n11\t\n12\t**Strategy**: Keyboard accessibility conformance for core Dashboard flows\n13\t**Triage**: Not below-threshold — although the strategy is S-sized with a single code\n14\tcomponent (Dashboard), the scope spans two architecturally distinct work streams:\n15\tkeyboard/focus remediation code in the Dashboard, and substantive accessibility\n16\tcontent authoring (VPAT rewrite and accessibility statement republish). The\n17\tmultiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition applies, so the strategy decomposes\n18\tinto separate code and content epics. No genuine unknowns: the strategy states the\n19\taudit report enumerates the exact defects per flow.\n20\t\n21\t## Epic List\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n24\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Keyboard operability and focus indicator remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | Update and republish accessibility conformance documentation (VPAT and accessibility statement) | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n27\t\n28\t## Dependency DAG\n29\t\n30\t```mermaid\n31\tgraph TD\n32\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9017-E001: Keyboard/focus remediation] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9017-E002: VPAT and docs republish]\n33\t```\n34\t\n35\t## DAG Justification\n36\t\n37\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n38\t|------|------|-----------|\n39\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by ALL Implementation epics) | The VPAT and accessibility statement must describe the fixed state, so the documentation epic is blocked by the Dashboard remediation epic. |\n40\t\n41\tNo other edges: the remediation epic is a single logical change (see HLR Traceability)\n42\tand there are no external dependencies, investigations, or onboarding chains — the\n43\tDashboard is an existing, Konflux-onboarded component per architecture context.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n46\t\n47\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n48\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n49\t| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Keyboard operability of the four audited flows. |\n50\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | `bundled` — consistent focus indicators edit the same flows, components, and UI surfaces as the HLR-1 focus-trap/unreachable-control fixes (same modal dialogs, same forms, same CSS/patternfly surface). Splitting HLR-2 into its own epic would double-touch the same files and produce two epics building the same surface, so it stays bundled with HLR-1. Both are P1, so no deferral signal is lost. |\n51\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | VPAT and accessibility statement update, technical review, and republish. |\n52\t\n53\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n54\t\n55\t## Health Warnings\n56\t\n57\t- **Missing strategy sections**: The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n58\t  Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), and no Non-Functional\n59\t  Requirements section. Epic acceptance criteria below were derived from the HLRs and\n60\t  the problem statement; the strategy should ideally be back-filled with explicit ACs.\n61\t- **Team inference**: The strategy does not state owners. The Dashboard epic is\n62\t  assigned to RHOAI Dashboard per the architecture context file\n63\t  (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`, owning team RHOAI Dashboard). The\n64\t  documentation epic is assigned to RHOAI Documentation as the Red Hat docs content\n65\t  process owner; the technical review AC routes Dashboard engineering sign-off. Verify\n66\t  both assignments with the strategy author.\n67\t- **Scope trap (low)**: The VPAT is a customer-facing conformance claim. Republishing\n68\t  it before the remediation is fully verified would create a compliance exposure — the\n69\t  E001 → E002 edge mitigates this, and the E002 acceptance criteria require the\n70\t  conformance statement to reflect only verified fixes.\n71\t- **Sizing**: E001 bundles the defects of four flows. The audit report enumerates the\n72\t  exact defects per flow; if the defect volume for a single flow exceeds roughly a\n73\t  sprint of remediation effort, re-split E001 by flow (each flow's fixes touch\n74\t  distinct Dashboard pages) rather than by HLR.\n75\t\n76\t## Tiered Delivery\n77\t\n78\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing; both epics are\n79\tinternal and sequential by nature (docs describe the fixed state).\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1f8d316935a9a76","agent_id":"a79b34fa455aac525","session_id":"73162c37-dfef-4424-b9a3-b9a22025d187","uuid":"11d5d3e3-9dab-4216-aced-fc2a16bc11d0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:53:03.467Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9395bd3289926d98","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
